(4557275, 654500, 30982, '<td valign="top">It''s nice to see that real silver still exists somewhere - I trust these are family heirlooms?  I don''t believe I''ve ever used actual silverware, only the stainless steel variety.  I like the varied stages of tarnish - somehow gives it more history than if they were all nicely polished and shiny.</td>', 'It''s nice to see that real silver still exists somewhere - I trust these are family heirlooms?  I don''t believe I''ve ever used actual silverware, only the stainless steel variety.  I like the varied stages of tarnish - somehow gives it more history than if they were all nicely polished and shiny.', '2008-03-12 07:27:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557286, 652547, 69246, '<td valign="top">AH!! There is where yours was hiding!  Nicely done, 83/210..not bad for a first timer....and definately not what I was expecting!!  I actually voted high on this one....<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-12 07:32:51.</i></td>', 'AH!! There is where yours was hiding!  Nicely done, 83/210..not bad for a first timer....and definately not what I was expecting!!  I actually voted high on this one.... Welcome to DPC....', '2008-03-12 07:32:32.000000', '2008-03-12 07:32:51.000000', 0),
(4557287, 653460, 30982, '<td valign="top">The trick is you hide the bowl part of the spoon and only photograph the handle... :-)  I know what you mean, though - it''s hard to avoid the reflections since spoons make such good but warped mirrors.  A simple elegant setting - the reflected blue makes me think of summer for some reason, and the promise of ice cream in that dish behind the spoon.  From a compositional standpoint, I think the horizontal line between the spoon and the glassware is an interruption of sorts - I think that''s where the table surface changes, yes?</td>', 'The trick is you hide the bowl part of the spoon and only photograph the handle... :-)  I know what you mean, though - it''s hard to avoid the reflections since spoons make such good but warped mirrors.  A simple elegant setting - the reflected blue makes me think of summer for some reason, and the promise of ice cream in that dish behind the spoon.  From a compositional standpoint, I think the horizontal line between the spoon and the glassware is an interruption of sorts - I think that''s where the table surface changes, yes?', '2008-03-12 07:32:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557292, 654334, 30982, '<td valign="top">Ah!  A spoon!  I never did figure out what the reflecting surface was.  Very nice abstract and ''grats on the Eyewave ribbon!</td>', 'Ah!  A spoon!  I never did figure out what the reflecting surface was.  Very nice abstract and ''grats on the Eyewave ribbon!', '2008-03-12 07:34:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557307, 654518, 55956, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the explanation, good idea!</td>', 'Thanks for the explanation, good idea!', '2008-03-12 07:42:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557319, 654511, 56658, '<td valign="top">very cool shot and great finish. great job!</td>', 'very cool shot and great finish. great job!', '2008-03-12 07:53:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557325, 654054, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh - I noticed at least two folks thought that this looked like either exercising or gymnastics - I had similar thoughts.  They look like they''re doing backbends!  Maybe a little plain in presentation and I think it would have been more striking on a more reflective surface and perhaps at an angle instead of straight across.</td>', 'Heh - I noticed at least two folks thought that this looked like either exercising or gymnastics - I had similar thoughts.  They look like they''re doing backbends!  Maybe a little plain in presentation and I think it would have been more striking on a more reflective surface and perhaps at an angle instead of straight across.', '2008-03-12 07:58:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557331, 654050, 30982, '<td valign="top">This made me smile - and I thought it might have been someone else''s who does very fun things with peeps.  As for the flat light - I think it may be more of a need to whiten the white of your background.  One way to do that is with a levels adjustment; another may be with the white balance in RAW if you''re shooting in RAW.  You did a good job of avoiding reflections and hot spots on the silverware itself (hard to do!) and I really do like the color added by the peeps.</td>', 'This made me smile - and I thought it might have been someone else''s who does very fun things with peeps.  As for the flat light - I think it may be more of a need to whiten the white of your background.  One way to do that is with a levels adjustment; another may be with the white balance in RAW if you''re shooting in RAW.  You did a good job of avoiding reflections and hot spots on the silverware itself (hard to do!) and I really do like the color added by the peeps.', '2008-03-12 08:01:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557335, 654728, 30982, '<td valign="top">Silverware, as many discovered, is a nightmare with flash!  This shot made me hungry when voting.  I was suddenly craving chocolate covered strawberries... (and I do eat the strawberries!)  As you''ve discovered, some folks really don''t like colored borders.  It''s a matter of personal taste.  Overall well balanced, well composed - the crop of the fork worked just fine.</td>', 'Silverware, as many discovered, is a nightmare with flash!  This shot made me hungry when voting.  I was suddenly craving chocolate covered strawberries... (and I do eat the strawberries!)  As you''ve discovered, some folks really don''t like colored borders.  It''s a matter of personal taste.  Overall well balanced, well composed - the crop of the fork worked just fine.', '2008-03-12 08:04:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557346, 654317, 49804, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a start to your challenge entries, this is phenomenal, very nice job, and congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Wow, what a start to your challenge entries, this is phenomenal, very nice job, and congrats on the ribbon.', '2008-03-12 08:12:35.000000', NULL, 0),
